From 98d1fe22e454f6091bc6e2c0a3ea8d5e9f00ff82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:47:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] B70: shadow groundedness judges facts only, with
 coverage-based excerpts

Blind grading of 79 live Clef decisions (2026-10-07) found that rejections of
advice, absence, packet/meta and table-fragment sentences were never factual
errors, and that 20 of 52 rejections were excerpt-picker misses.

- shadow_claim_kind classifies table / absence / meta / advice / fact; only
  facts are sent to the judge (others are logged as skipped_non_fact). On the
  graded set: 25 of 26 plain facts kept, 37 of 41 non-facts skipped.
- shadow_select_evidence replaces fixed windows: greedy set cover over
  sentence-snapped segments of all cited pages, idf-weighted whole-token
  matching with light stemming, and number+unit terms ('4 hrs' == '4 hours';
  bare one/two-digit numbers no longer match on their own), within the
  1200-char budget; falls back to the page start when nothing matches.
- Graded set, kept claims, live Clef: supported facts accepted 19/24 (was
  17/24), unsupported rejected 10/14 (unchanged), agreement 29/38 at the 0.85
  threshold (was 27/38).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
